@startuml qwen3tts-speedup
title <b>qwen3tts: the components that buy 5x realtime</b>\n1612-word chapter, 100 segments, one M4 / 16 GB. Shipped RTF 0.252-0.261; 5x is RTF 0.200

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam titleFontSize 15
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 34
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #5A6B7A
  BackgroundColor #E8EDF2
  FontSize 12
}
skinparam noteFontSize 11

rectangle "**text::segment**\n1612 words -> 100 segments, max_chars each" as SEG
rectangle "**Talker::build_prompt**\nrole + ICL reference codes + speaker embedding" as PROMPT
rectangle "**Batch scheduler**\nbucket by shape, sort by length, chunk to 24 lanes" as SCHED #DDF3E0
rectangle "**Talker**  ---  RTF 0.187 of 0.260  (72%)\nQwen3 trunk 28L @ 2048, one step per 80 ms frame\n+ depth predictor 5L, 15 sequential AR steps per frame" as TALKER #DDF3E0
rectangle "**Codec decoder**  ---  RTF 0.073 of 0.260  (28%)\nRVQ dequant -> 8L transformer -> 2x (transconv + ConvNeXt)\n-> 4 decoder blocks -> SnakeBeta -> conv" as CODEC #DDF3E0
rectangle "**WAV 24 kHz**, 1920 samples per frame\nshipped: **RTF 0.260 = 3.9x realtime**" as WAV #D6E9F8

SEG --> PROMPT
PROMPT --> SCHED
SCHED --> TALKER : "groups of <= 24 equal-shape lanes"
TALKER --> CODEC : "[T, 16] codes per lane"
CODEC --> WAV

note right of SCHED #DDF3E0
  <b>Shipped, measured</b>
  * <b>Shape bucketing</b> by (prompt_len, trailing_len). The ICL block is fixed by the
    <i>voice</i>, so nearly every sentence buckets together -- no padding, no per-lane mask
  * <b>Length sort, then chunk.</b> A group runs as long as its longest lane. Unsorted,
    only 47-56% of lane-steps were useful on this chapter
end note

note right of TALKER #DDF3E0
  <b>Shipped, measured</b>
  * <b>f16 weights, not q8_0.</b> Only a dense GEMM shares one weight read across lanes:
    f16 amortises 7.4x, q8_0 just 1.1x. Chapter RTF 0.661 (q8_0) -> <b>0.260</b> (f16)
  * <b>Batched decode, 24 lanes.</b> Both transformers are bandwidth-bound on weight
    reads, so a lane costs little beyond a read the batch already pays
  * <b>In-place KV cache + tts_nn::attn.</b> slice_set instead of slice_assign, and
    attention reads the cache in place -- a narrow() span copied ~112 MB/step for nothing
  * <b>Predictor precompute.</b> 15 codebook tables concatenated (2 dispatches, not 45),
    resize folded in at load: ~126 MB/frame of weight traffic gone
  * <b>512-frame lane cap.</b> Sizes the KV cache; a lane that hits it is rerun with the
    full budget rather than shipped truncated
end note

note right of CODEC #DDF3E0
  <b>Shipped, measured</b>
  * <b>One call per utterance</b> over the concatenated frames, cut afterwards. Per-segment
    calls open with no left context and audibly change timbre
  * <b>Chunked, 300 frames + 25 of left context.</b> Bounds memory, and lets candle's Metal
    buffer pool recycle instead of paying every allocation cold
  * <b>tts_nn kernels.</b> Channels-last convs (k accumulating GEMMs, no im2col matrix),
    tap-major gather, fused SnakeBeta
end note

note left of TALKER #FDEBD0
  <b>Needed for 0.200 -- projected, no fixture</b>
  * <b>Continuous batching.</b> Refill a lane the moment
    it hits codec_eos. Today a finished lane keeps being
    stepped -- deliberately: repacking the cache cost
    more than the waste does at 24 lanes
  * <b>Wider batch, 32-48 lanes.</b> Still 3.40 ms/lane
    and falling at 24 (12.0x amortisation). Blocked by
    memory, not by returns: candle's Metal pool never
    releases, 11.1 GB peak on this chapter
end note

note left of CODEC #FDEBD0
  <b>Needed for 0.200 -- projected, no fixture</b>
  * <b>Codec kernel parity.</b> candle is 1.70-2.23x
    slower than torch on this codec, stable across every
    thermal state. The fused NLC path took audio8's codec
    0.260 -> 0.158; extending it over the transconv and
    ConvNeXt stages is the lever here
end note

note bottom of WAV #FFFDF0
  <b>Where the last 1.1x has to come from</b>
  |= |= talker |= codec |= total |= realtime |
  | shipped | 0.187 | 0.073 | <b>0.260</b> | 3.9x |
  | target | 0.145 | 0.055 | <b>0.200</b> | <b>5.0x</b> |

  The talker is 72% of the cost, so the talker levers are the ones that can carry this. The codec cannot
  do it alone: driving 0.073 to <i>zero</i> still leaves 0.187, which only reaches 5.3x if the talker holds exactly.

  <b>Refuted, do not retry:</b> f32 weights (RTF <b>6.25</b> at 6.97 GB resident), batching q8_0 (1.02 against 0.79),
  device-side sampling, an f16 codec decoder, ONNX Runtime, CoreML.
end note

@enduml
